First:  I used to play Moria.  I liked it, but it is an overall inferior 
game to NetHack.  It does have some neat features that might be nice to 
see in a next version of NetHack...
	1.  Moria seems to treat "running" better than NH.  In Moria, the 
"."  command functions like the "g" NH command except that Moria has 
options for continuing to "run" around corners, through doors, etc.  NH 
seems to only go in a straight line, which is nice but not as useful as 
it probably could be...
	2.  In NetHack, if you want to know about something in a space in 
the room that you are not stepping on, you have to use the "/" directive 
and then place the cursor.  That's nice, but Moria has a similar, 
directional "examine" command (I think it is "x" or "X" or something) 
which is a lot more convenient.  
	3.  In Moria, you can rest for a given number of rounds.  This is 
similar to "n(number)." in NH.  The problem is that a monster can wander 
in and barf fire or shoot arrows at you before the "." terminates.  This 
can be VERY bad. In Moria, the rest is terminated when something in your 
line of sight moves. That way, you can get the jump on a monster 
entering the room.  (The  problem with NH doing this is that you pet 
tends to move :-) ).  Because of NetHack's lack of warning of a 
monster's approach, I tend to push and  hold down the "." key to rest, 
and because of the weak "running" feature in NH, I tend to flood the 
buffer with movement commands.  I wish I had a  Zorkmid for every 
Floating Eye I accidentally ran into this way.  Also, Moria has a "rest 
until HP and Mana restored" feature which would be VERY nice in NetHack.
	4.  I think Moria's "line of sight" algorithm is better that 
NetHack's, but I can't prove it :-).  Infravision in NetHack would be 
nice.
	5.  NetHack is much better than Moria at handling item 
identification and providing the user with a list of "known" items.  
Moria, on the other  hand, has a very nice feature whereby you can get a 
list of information that you have "discovered" about the monsters you 
have killed.  It would be grand to identify a kobold and get a little 
paragraph telling you it's relative speed, it's alignment, and that it's 
corpse is poisonous (it you've eaten kobold before).
	6.  Moria has a "search mode" which is like automatically 
searching after every move.  That would be nice to see in NetHack.
	7.  (Someone mentioned this recently) It would be nice to be able 
to  switch between a primary and secondary weapon with a single command.
	8.  I wish you could buy oil and apply it to lamps to recharge 
them.
	
