I got really sick of carrying lots of weapons of various types dropped 
by low level monsters like orcs.  But, if I left the weapons in a room, 
I usually ended up having them used against me by a newly created 
monster who wandered through and picked it up.  So here's my solution.  
Please write in if you have more.
	I put as much as I can into chests.  Monsters don't seem to be 
able to  open chests.
	or... I engrave Elbereth well and dump the stuff there.
	or (I like this one the best) I take all the weapons I don't want 
and  use them to inscribe "1234567890" on the floor.  This tells me the 
enchantment (+1 can inscribe the whole thing, +0 gets to "7", and -1 
either gets to "5" or says its too dull already (I can't remember)).  It 
also makes the weapon -1 to hit and -1 to damage.  After engraving, I 
#name the weapon "sucker" so I don't pick it up again accidentally.  
	There's nothing more ironically pleasing than to be "almost hit" 
by an orcish dagger named "sucker"
 
